model {
  extend basalt.build {
    metadata {
      constraint "Acceptance journeys intercept the public app-account creation request and retain its creation identity across a lost response. Query holds precede refresh and use the same undeclared-response failure inside or outside a batch before proving retry; loading assertions wait for an observable loading state. Display, menu and tool expectations follow their declared contracts. Only the controlled PostgreSQL startup-failure fixture normalizes ECONNRESET. Managed MCP signing keys survive the runtime-control wrapper and cross the private redacted fixture channel, never run metadata or exported evidence. Existing authority, persistence, recovery assertions and deadlines remain intact."
    }
  }
}
